@page "/bio"

<PageTitle>Bio | Turley Richards | 50 Years in Music</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="The life and career of Turley Richards — born in Charleston, WV, signed by 7 major labels, performing with Aretha Franklin, Miles Davis, and more over a 50-year career." />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Bio | Turley Richards" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="From Charleston, WV to national television — read the full story of Turley Richards' 50-year music career." />
    <meta property="og:image" content="/images/turleyblackwhite.jpeg" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="/bio" />
</HeadContent>

<!-- Bio Hero -->
<section class="bio-hero-section" aria-label="Biography header">
    <div class="container py-5">
        <div class="row align-items-center g-4">
            <div class="col-md-5 text-center">
                <img src="/images/turleyblackwhite.jpeg"
                     alt="Turley Richards performing early in his career"
                     class="img-fluid rounded-4 shadow bio-hero-img" />
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-7">
                <h1 class="section-heading">Turley Richards</h1>
                <p class="fs-4 fst-italic mb-3">Vocalist · Producer · Songwriter · Vocal Coach</p>
                <p class="fs-5">
                    Born and raised in <strong>Charleston, West Virginia</strong>, Turley Richards discovered
                    his gift for music at an early age. Despite losing most of his sight in adulthood,
                    Turley refused to let adversity define him — instead channeling every challenge into
                    a deeper, more soulful artistic expression that would span over five decades.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Career Narrative -->
<section class="bio-career-section" aria-labelledby="career-heading">
    <div class="container py-5">
        <h2 id="career-heading" class="section-heading mb-4">A Career Spanning Five Decades</h2>
        <div class="row g-4">
            <div class="col-md-8">
                <p class="fs-5">
                    Turley's career began taking shape in the 1960s, when his powerful voice and natural
                    showmanship attracted the attention of major industry players. He went on to be signed
                    by <strong>seven major record labels</strong> — Warner Brothers, Columbia, Atlantic,
                    Epic, MGM, and 20th Century Fox — a testament to the lasting appeal of his artistry.
                </p>
                <p class="fs-5">
                    Along the way, Turley appeared on some of the most iconic stages and television programs
                    in America: <em>Dick Clark's American Bandstand</em>, <em>The Tonight Show</em>,
                    <em>The Merv Griffin Show</em>, and <em>The David Frost Show</em>. His live performances
                    took him to stages across the country alongside legends like Aretha Franklin, Miles Davis,
                    Tony Bennett, The 5th Dimension, and dozens more.
                </p>
                <p class="fs-5">
                    As a songwriter, Turley has written and published over <strong>600 songs</strong>,
                    weaving together the soul, gospel, R&amp;B, and pop influences that define his sound.
                    His latest work, <em>The Man In Me</em>, is a compilation spanning 1970–2020 that
                    reflects the full arc of his extraordinary journey.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4 text-center">
                <img src="/images/turleybillygraham.jpg"
                     alt="Turley Richards at an early career event"
                     class="img-fluid rounded-4 shadow mb-3" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Teaching & Legacy -->
<section class="bio-teaching-section" aria-labelledby="teaching-heading">
    <div class="container py-5">
        <div class="row align-items-center g-4">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h2 id="teaching-heading" class="section-heading">Giving Back Through Music</h2>
                <p class="fs-5">
                    Today, Turley channels decades of professional knowledge into coaching the next
                    generation of musicians. Working out of his <strong>professional 12-track studio</strong>
                    in Louisville, KY, he offers vocal coaching, songwriting instruction, studio recording,
                    music therapy, and music business consulting — drawing on 40+ years of hands-on
                    experience in New York, Los Angeles, and Nashville.
                </p>
                <p class="fs-5">
                    His mission is simple: pass on the craft, the discipline, and the joy that music
                    has given him, so that the next generation can build something equally extraordinary.
                </p>
                <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-4">
                    <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
                        <i class="bi bi-envelope me-2"></i>Get In Touch
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="/images/turleydailycup.jpeg"
                     alt="Turley Richards"
                     class="img-fluid rounded-4 shadow" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

